      <!-- ALIGNMENT vs GHYaf3-d1e633 (Oyta abbreviatio). 126 sources -> 36 targets, all 36 targets
           referenced, 61 sources mapped, 65 dropped. Q2 (utrum profectus vel augmentum gratiae fiat
           per compositionem novae gratiae cum gratia praecedenti). Extremely compressed, comparable
           to Q4 (74->15); this text runs the "8 conclusiones + objections + responses ad Nm" article
           structure and Oyta keeps that skeleton but drops a huge share of the supporting arguments
           and objections under each conclusion. INITIAL PASS from close reading; not yet split
           fold-by-fold with user.

           STRUCTURE: d114 opening question; d136/d143 intro to the 8 conclusiones; d164-d652 the 8
           conclusiones themselves plus their supporting Item-arguments (heavily compressed; see
           huge folds below); d785-d1012 the "ad primum...ad argumentum principale" response section,
           which mostly maps close to 1:1 once matched by content (source's own ad-N numbering does
           NOT line up with target's ad-N numbering, since Oyta silently drops many objections/
           responses; matches here were made by content, not by number).

           HUGE FOLDS (target <- N sources; splitting candidates):
           d652 <- 7: d2095,d2103,d2172,d2275,d2308,d2383,d2463 (light/mirror-reflection and
           frigiditas/caliditas thought experiments; this is the single densest paragraph in the
           file and very likely under-resolved; several nearby sources, e.g. d2205,d2242,d2334,
           d2372,d2441, may belong here too but weren't confidently placed).
           d202 <- 5: d373,d415(partial),d464,d481,d494.
           d574 <- 5: d1719,d1747,d1890,d1905,d1937(partial).
           d290 <- 4: d545,d587,d603(partial),d707(partial).
           d402 <- 4: d1188,d1199,d1360,d1449; this one is the least certain: target's text runs
           "quarta conclusio...contra pe. aureo....Sexta conclusio" with NO "quinta conclusio" ever
           named, meaning either quinta was silently dropped/absorbed or one of the sources placed
           here actually belongs to a missing quinta. Sources d1232,d1255,d1272,d1316,d1340,d1402
           (all about unibility/distinctness of caritas-parts, between 4a and 6a in the source) were
           NOT placed and are current DROPPED; worth checking against d402 again.
           d350 <- 3: d1031,d1055,d1071(partial).
           d853 <- 3: d2766,d2819(partial),d2846(partial-head only).

           MULTI-TARGET single sources: d1504->506,526 (7a/8a conclusio boundary, source paragraph
           spans both); d2846->853,875,882 (one large response paragraph spans three target
           paragraphs; the reverse-fold pattern also seen in Q3).

           MASSIVE DROP (65 sources, far more than usual): the entire block d208-d353 (supporting
           arguments for conclusio 1 beyond what d202 uses) is dropped wholesale; likewise d626/d648,
           d760-d902 (substantial-forms/elements tangent before conclusio 2), d958-d1121/d1170
           (extra support for conclusio 1 continued oddly late; needs re-checking, may be
           misordered in this transcription pass), most of d1232-d1843 (unibility-of-parts material
           around conclusio 4-6), d1960-d2064 (motus-mensuratur-instanti tangent), d2123-d2372 and
           d2441 (extra light/lumen arguments not absorbed into d652), d2594/d2780/d2798/d2906-d2953
           (editorial asides and stub cross-references), and a long stretch of unlabelled or
           stub "ad Nm: idem ac ad Xm" responses near the end (d3054-d3608 minus the ones used for
           d908/d916/d925/d932/d945/d954/d974) which appear to be genuinely dropped short responses.

           NOT YET reviewed fold-by-fold with user; HTML review pending. -->
